{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BaryonWeight.beta4_hook","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.beta4_hook","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.beta4_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.beta4_hook","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BaryonWeight/beta4_hook.lean#L40-L68","doc":"**Proposition** (hook-weight derivation).\n\nThe coefficient of the hook invariant $\\Phi_4$ in the four-channel mass\nformula is\n\n$$\n  \\beta_4 = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\, w_{[2,2]}(4)\n          = -\\frac{\\dim_q([2,2])^2}{2\\,[4]_q!}\n          \\approx -0.083 ,\n$$\n\nwhere $w_{[2,2]}(4) = \\dim_q([2,2])^2 / [4]_q!$ is the Wedderburn-Artin\nweight of the hook partition $[2,2]$ in $H_4(R, q)$, the baryon's\ninternal Hecke algebra (3 quarks + gluon = 4 strands).\n\nThe identity `β₄ = −½·w_{[2,2]}` is **derived** by `ring` from the\ndefinition of `β₄`; the numerical bound `|β₄ + 0.083| < 0.005` is\n**derived** from the empirical weight bound `|w_{[2,2]} − 0.166| < 0.01`\ncarried by `[Hook22Weight]` — the lone open input. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hook-weight-derivation","label":"prop:hook-weight-derivation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hook-weight-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.beta4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.beta4","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BaryonWeight/beta4_hook.lean#L36-L38","doc":"The hook coefficient `β₄`, **defined** as `−½·w_{[2,2]}(4)` (not\nassumed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight.w_22_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight.w_22_approx","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BaryonWeight/beta4_hook.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The `H₄(R, q)` decomposition at the substrate yields\n`w_{[2,2]}(4) ≈ 0.166`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight.w_22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight.w_22","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BaryonWeight/beta4_hook.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Wedderburn-Artin weight `w_{[2,2]}(4) = dim_q([2,2])² / [4]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BaryonWeight/beta4_hook.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.Hook22Weight","kind":"class","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BaryonWeight/beta4_hook.lean#L23-L34","doc":"The one genuinely-open input for the `β₄` hook coefficient: the\nempirical value of the Wedderburn-Artin weight\n`w_{[2,2]}(4) = dim_q([2,2])² / [4]_q! ≈ 0.166` read off the\n`H₄(R, q)` decomposition at the substrate `q₀`.  A categorical\nderivation of the numerical value is open (the §3b conjectural\nhypothesis); the hook identity below is *derived* from it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}